    "answer": "oep-ke-keph-pharmacy-018-option-1",
    "explanation": "Furosemide is a loop diuretic that inhibits the Na+/K+/2Cl- co-transporter in the thick ascending limb of the loop of Henle, producing powerful diuresis. It can cause hypokalaemia and ototoxicity at high doses.",
