    "explanation": "Omalizumab prevents IgE from binding high-affinity FcεRI receptors on mast cells and basophils. P2-Q1 B Tamsulosin selectively targets uroselective alpha-1A receptors in the prostate and bladder neck. P2-Q2 B Barbiturates prolong the duration of GABA-mediated Cl- channel opening (benzodiazepines increase frequency). P2-Q3 B SSRIs (sertraline, fluoxetine, escitalopram) selectively block SERT with far better safety than TCAs/MAOIs. P2-Q4 A Clindamycin inhibits 50S ribosomal translocation and is a classic trigger for C. difficile pseudomembranous colitis. P2-Q5 B Fondaparinux is a synthetic pentasaccharide that selectively inhibits Factor Xa via antithrombin. P2-Q6 B Both thioamides inhibit thyroid peroxidase; PTU also inhibits peripheral T4-to-T3 conversion. P2-Q7 B Ondansetron blocks 5-HT3 receptors in the GI tract and chemoreceptor trigger zone (CTZ). P2-Q8 B Cyclosporine forms a complex with cyclophilin that inhibits calcineurin phosphatase activity. P2-Q9 C Aliskiren directly inhibits renin enzyme activity. P2- B SGLT2 inhibitors and GLP-1 RAs demonstrate proven cardiovascular and heart-failure Q10 mortality reductions. P2- B IV Artesunate is first-line for severe malaria across all patient groups, followed by a full Q11 oral ACT course. P2- B Multivalent cations (Ca2+, Mg2+, Al3+, Fe2+) chelate fluoroquinolones; separate doses Q12 by at least 2–4 hours. P2- B IV loop diuretics promote rapid venodilation and natriuresis to reduce pulmonary Q13 congestion. P2- B UFH prolongs aPTT (target typically 1.5–2.5× control), whereas warfarin is monitored via Q14 PT/INR. P2- B Transaminases >5× ULN (or >3× ULN with jaundice/symptoms) require immediate Q15 interruption of hepatotoxic TB drugs. P2- B Bupropion (NDRI) aids smoking cessation and lacks SSRI-associated sexual dysfunction Q16 (contraindicated in seizure disorders). P2- B IM Epinephrine (0.3–0.5 mg in adults) rapidly reverses bronchospasm, vasodilation, and Q17 laryngeal edema. P2- B Low K+ and low Mg2+ prolong ventricular repolarization and trigger torsades de pointes. Q18 P2- B Claviceps purpurea (ergot fungus) parasitizes rye and other cereal grains. Q19 P2- A Indian snakeroot (Rauwolfia serpentina) yields reserpine, ajmaline, and serpentine. Q20 P2- B Saponins are amphiphilic glycosides that lower surface tension and produce stable foam. Q21 P2- A Colchicum autumnale seeds and corms contain colchicine. Q22 P2- B Free anthraquinones turn pink/red in alkaline ammonia solution. Q23 P2- B Eugenol makes up 70–90% of clove bud volatile oil. Q24 P2- A Podophyllum resin yields podophyllotoxin, used topically for warts and semi-synthetically Q25 for etoposide. P2- B Isoprene units (IPP and DMAPP) are synthesized via the mevalonate and MEP pathways. Q26 P2- B Glidants coat particle surfaces to improve powder flowability; lubricants reduce punch/die Q27 friction. P2- B Lyophilization preserves thermolabile biologics/injectables via low-temperature vacuum Q28 sublimation. P2- C 5 g / 100 mL × 120 mL = 6.0 g. Q29 P2- A Type I borosilicate glass prevents alkali leaching into injectable solutions. Q30 P2- B Paraben esters act as broad-spectrum antimicrobial preservatives (often combined for Q31 synergistic solubility). P2- B Compressed or liquefied gas propellants provide driving pressure and atomization. Q32 P2- B USP Apparatus 2 is the standard rotating paddle apparatus for tablets and capsules. Q33 P2- B Total daily dose = 8 kg × 40 mg/kg = 320 mg/day; divided every 12 hours = 160 mg per Q34 dose. P2- B Temperature fluctuations dissolve small particles, which recrystallize onto larger ones, Q35 causing caking. P2- B Rf = d_spot / d_solvent, always ranging between 0 and 1. Q36 P2- B The strained beta-lactam amide bond mimics D-Ala-D-Ala and irreversibly acylates Q37 transpeptidase PBPs. P2- B C-6 fluorine increases gyrase potency ~10-fold; C-7 piperazine expands Gram-negative Q38 (Pseudomonas) activity. P2- B Mass spectrometry ionizes molecules and separates fragment ions by m/z ratio. Q39 P2- B Stereoselectivity separates antitussive action (dextro-isomer) from mu-opioid analgesia/ Q40 dependence (levo-isomer). P2- B Eriochrome Black T forms a wine-red complex with Mg2+/Ca2+ that turns pure blue at the Q41 EDTA endpoint. P2- B Diazotization followed by coupling with N-(1-naphthyl)ethylenediamine forms an azo dye Q42 for assay. P2- B Diacetylation increases lipophilicity, accelerating crossing of the blood-brain barrier before Q43 deacetylation to morphine. P2- B Gravimetry relies on precise mass measurement of an isolated, stable precipitate. Q44 P2- B CFR = (Deaths due to disease / Total diagnosed cases of that disease) × 100%, measuring Q45 disease virulence/severity. P2- A Attack rate is a cumulative incidence measure used during acute outbreaks. Q46 P2- B Confounders (e.g., smoking when studying coffee and lung cancer) mix effects unless Q47 controlled via randomization, matching, or regression. P2- C Primary prevents onset (vaccines); secondary detects early asymptomatic disease; Q48 tertiary reduces complications/disability. P2- B RR = Incidence_exposed / Incidence_unexposed (RR > 1 indicates increased risk). Q49 P2- B Group-level correlations (e.g., national sugar sales vs. diabetes) may not hold for Q50 individuals. P2- B Specificity = True Negatives / (True Negatives + False Positives), ruling IN disease when Q51 positive (SpPIn). P2- B Attributable risk (RD) shows the absolute public health impact of removing an exposure. Q52 P2- B Informed consent upholds participant autonomy under the Declaration of Helsinki and Q53 Kenyan NACOSTI/ERC rules. P2- B ITT preserves baseline randomization balance and reflects real-world clinical effectiveness. Q54 P2- B Pearson's r assesses linear correlation for parametric continuous variables; Spearman's ρ Q55 is non-parametric. P2- B Type II error (β) is a false negative; increasing sample size reduces β and increases power Q56 (1 - β). P2- B Histograms and boxplots depict continuous distributions, medians, IQRs, and outliers. Q57 P2- B Forest plots summarize effect sizes and precision across multiple pooled studies. Q58 P2- B Mann-Whitney U compares medians/ranks of two independent non-normal groups; Q59 Wilcoxon signed-rank is for paired data. P2- B Allocation concealment (e.g., centralized randomization) prevents selection bias at Q60 enrollment. This is for informational purposes only. For medical advice or diagnosis, consult a professional. AI responses may include mistakes.",
